This test has a race condition. The main thread sets `deletedAll.set(true)` and immediately proceeds to the assertion. The reader thread might still be executing its final `managedRealm.admin().groups().groups(...)` call. If an exception is thrown during that final call, the main thread might have already executed the assertion and the test would incorrectly pass.

To make the test robust, you should store the thread in a variable and wait for it to complete before checking for exceptions.

Example:
```java
        Thread readerThread = new Thread(() -> {
            // ... reader loop
        });
        readerThread.start();

        // delete groups
        groupUuuids.forEach(groupUuid -> {
            managedRealm.admin().groups().group(groupUuid).remove();
        });
        deletedAll.set(true);

        try {
            readerThread.join(); // Wait for the reader thread to finish
        } catch (InterruptedException e) {
            Thread.currentThread().interrupt();
            fail("Test interrupted");
        }

        assertThat(caughtExceptions, Matchers.empty());
```
